# Kasumi (Anatdx/Kasumi) — obj-y in-tree port

config KASUMI
	bool "Kasumi root-hiding framework (in-tree obj-y port)"
	depends on ARM64 && !MODULES
	select KPROBES
	select KALLSYMS
	select KALLSYMS_ALL
	select DEBUG_KERNEL
	default n
	help
	  In-tree obj-y port of Anatdx/Kasumi (upstream: LKM). Provides
	  syscall-table TSR + ftrace/kretprobe hook stack for mount /
	  getattr / dents / xattr concealment on Android.

	  Bootstraps at late_initcall via kprobe-on-kallsyms_lookup_name to
	  resolve non-exported kernel symbols. The optional ftrace fallback
	  layer is auto-gated in-source by CONFIG_DYNAMIC_FTRACE (no build
	  dependency here — TSR is the primary carrier and needs no ftrace).

	  This entry uses `select` (not `depends on`) for KPROBES /
	  KALLSYMS / KALLSYMS_ALL / DEBUG_KERNEL because:
	    * KPROBES in stock arch/Kconfig carries `depends on MODULES`, a
	      stale legacy restriction. SULTAN17 uses INTEGRATE_MODULES=y
	      (mutually exclusive with MODULES per kernel/module/Kconfig),
	      so a plain `depends on KPROBES` would silently drop CONFIG_KASUMI.
	      arm64 unconditionally builds module.o (arch/arm64/kernel/Makefile
	      line 37), so module_alloc() — kprobes' only MODULES-adjacent
	      link-time dependency — exists regardless of CONFIG_MODULES.
	      `select KPROBES` is therefore safe here.
	    * KALLSYMS_ALL carries `depends on DEBUG_KERNEL && KALLSYMS`
	      (init/Kconfig). DEBUG_KERNEL is absent from gs201_defconfig,
	      so a plain `depends on KALLSYMS_ALL` would also silently drop
	      CONFIG_KASUMI. `select KALLSYMS_ALL` + `select DEBUG_KERNEL`
	      forces both on for our build.
	  See /workspace/kasumi-configstick.md for the full autopsy.

	  Non-stock detection surface: /proc/config.gz reveals CONFIG_KASUMI=y,
	  System.map exposes kasumi_* symbols (address-taken subset kept under
	  GCC-LTO). See /workspace/kasumi-recon.md §5-6 for symbol/API audit.

	  Say N unless you know exactly what this is.
